course: dictionary
lesson: 11325
title: Yoga and its two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is needed. «Ring-tailed lemurs sit in the morning sun with their arms out like children doing yoga.» The stretching and the arms held out tell you that yoga here is a kind of exercise, where you stretch, hold your body in special positions and breathe slowly.
explain: Yoga is also an old way of thinking that began in India, and it includes meditation, which means sitting quietly to calm your mind. So if a story is about a person sitting still and thinking calm thoughts for a long time, the context points to the older meaning. Look at the words around the word and decide which meaning fits.
explain: Check with a swap. «The lemurs sit in the morning sun and do yoga» still makes sense, so yoga works as an activity. Notice too that yoga is uncountable: we say «do yoga» or «a yoga class», not «two yogas» when we mean the exercise.
fact: Yoga means a kind of exercise with stretching, special body positions and slow breathing.
fact: Yoga is also an old way of thinking and meditation that began in India.
fact: «A yoga pose» is one special body position, such as a stretch you hold for a few breaths.
fact: «A yoga mat» is the mat you stand, sit or lie on while doing yoga, and «a yoga class» is a lesson led by a teacher.
fact: In PE and health lessons, yoga is an example of exercise that builds flexibility and balance.
exercise: «Ring-tailed lemurs sit in the morning sun with their arms out like children doing yoga.» What is yoga in this sentence? | Hot chocolate | A game played with a ball | *A kind of exercise with stretching and slow breathing | A type of sunhat
exercise: In PE lessons, yoga is an example of exercise that builds what? | Loud singing | *Flexibility and balance | Speed in running races | Spelling and reading
exercise: Which phrase means one special body position in yoga? | a yoga mat | *a yoga pose | a yoga teacher | a yoga class
test: Before stretching at home, Ella unrolls her ___ on the floor. | yoga teacher | yoga pose | *yoga mat | yoga class
test: Yoga began as an old way of thinking in which country? | Africa | Madagascar | *India | Scotland
exam: Jayden says, «Yoga is just a dance.» Using the lesson, what is the best reply? | *No, yoga is mainly stretching, holding poses and slow breathing, not dancing | Yes, it is a dance with music and jumping | Yoga is a kind of food eaten by lemurs
